Media Queries are about defining different style rules for different devices (screens, tablets, mobile phones, etc.). You can learn more 
Media Queries in ourMedia Queries Chapter.

Now we want to set one variable value for screens below 450px wide, and 
another variable value for screens above 450px wide.

Here, we first declare a new local variable named --fontsize for the.containerclass. We set its value to 20 pixels. Then, we create a@mediarule that says "When the browser's width 
is 450px or wider, change the --fontsize variable value of the.containerclass to 40px.":

